& [ObservedGap] has two legitimate commit identities
  + runtime checkpoint identifies the executable implementation being measured
  + corpus design checkpoint identifies what implementation context informed test authorship
  + current calibration configuration has only checkpoint_commit and requires corpus designed_against_commit to equal it
  + additive runtime changes therefore force either a false corpus relabel or a duplicate corpus with unchanged test payloads

& [CandidateCorrection] is non-authoritative until SJS
  + add corpus_design_commit as an exact configuration identity
  + retain checkpoint_commit for the runtime under test
  + validate corpus designed_against_commit against corpus_design_commit rather than runtime checkpoint
  + emit both identities in health and new evidence
  + preserve verification compatibility for already archived evidence

& [HonestyBoundary] distinguishes reuse from authorship
  + a reused regression corpus remains authored against its original design checkpoint
  + a runtime result never implies the corpus was newly authored for that runtime
  + corpus raw bytes ID and digest remain unchanged
  + this change does not make same-project evidence independent or held out

& [CompatibilityIntent] is narrow
  + active corpus procedures schemas and expected arguments remain unchanged
  + runtime deployment identity updates independently
  + old evidence remains byte-verifiable without migration
  + no inference threshold catalogue model or effect changes
